   "level": 2,
   "text": "Double angle formulae"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "What are the double angle formulae?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- The **double angle formulae** are derived from the 'A+B' versions of the **compound angle formulae**:\n\n  - `sin open parentheses 2 A close parentheses identical to 2 sin A cos A`\n  - $\\mathrm{cos}(2A)\\equiv\\mathrm{cos}^{2}A-\\mathrm{sin}^{2}A$\n  \n    - $\\mathrm{cos}(2A)\\equiv2\\mathrm{cos}^{2}A-1$\n    - $\\mathrm{cos}(2A)\\equiv1-2\\mathrm{sin}^{2}A$\n  - $\\mathrm{tan}(2A)\\equiv\\frac{2\\mathrm{tan}A}{1-\\mathrm{tan}^{2}A}$"
  },
